WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.664
Today your child reads words with two sounds.

2
00:00:03.114 --> 00:00:09.926
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:10.426 --> 00:00:13.005
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

4
00:00:13.505 --> 00:00:14.829
This is today's page.

5
00:00:15.279 --> 00:00:19.178
Most children say the two sounds with a gap between them. Like this.

6
00:00:22.251 --> 00:00:27.161
With a gap, the word does not come. So hold the first sound until you reach the second.

7
00:00:29.053 --> 00:00:29.974
The word is at.

8
00:00:30.874 --> 00:00:35.424
Put your finger on the dot under the word. Slide it along the arrow as you say it.

9
00:00:35.874 --> 00:00:39.394
Do the first word yourself. Then your child does the same word.

10
00:00:39.844 --> 00:00:40.854
Here is one more.

11
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.010
The word is in.

12
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:49.913
If your child stops between the sounds, slide your finger with theirs and say it together.

13
00:00:50.363 --> 00:00:54.346
Then they read the words again, a little more smoothly, and trace three of them.
